  "title": "Identifying Triggers and Patterns",
  "content": "Every parent has emotional triggers—moments that spark frustration, fear, or anger more quickly than others. These triggers often come from past experiences, stress, or unmet needs. When parents understand their triggers, they can respond with intention instead of reacting automatically.\n\nThis lesson helps parents identify patterns in their emotional responses. For example, some parents react strongly to defiance because they were punished harshly as children. Others become overwhelmed by noise, chaos, or time pressure. Recognising these patterns is the first step toward change.\n\nWhen parents understand their triggers, they can prepare for difficult moments, use regulation strategies earlier, and communicate their needs more clearly.",
